Although I have left neovim for experimenting with kakoune and helix a few months ago, I'm saying this as someone who used it for years and deeply appreciates it.

from a technical standpoint:

just delete the quote bro, it serves no purpose and only serves to associate this project with DHH, which only harms the project and its community.

you gain absolutely nothing by choosing to keep it.

from an political standpoint:

Tell me what company you keep, and I will tell you what you are.

@mfhens Even Hitler didn't shout all the time. The nazis were mostly talking about the pernicious influence of the Jewish population and how the foreign influence was dangerous to German-ness etc. The veneer of politeness was important to them, at least for a while, because it legitimizes what is ultimately an illegitimate political position. (As per the paradox of tolerance, I don't think fascism is really a political position at all, much less one to be tolerated.) 

That said, I don't think there's much politeness either in equating the Roma with wolves that should be shot. It is pretty far out there, in fact it's _very_ close to Mussolini. Remigration is just one of many boxes ticked in his blog posts - dehumanization (they're dirty and even shit everywhere!), the apocalyptic rhetoric (Europe will collapse unless!) and even comparisons with animals. I think the boxes are well taken care of.

Let's also keep in mind that quoting a testimonial from the creator of the set of insecure dotfiles called Omarchy should be a [source of embarrassment](https://indieweb.social/@sstephenson/117157341360479277), not pride.
